# Paytm Build for India AI Hackathon — Team Workspace

Goal: win the Bengaluru finale.
Status: **Round 1 SHORTLISTED ✅** · finale vertical slice **BUILT + VERIFIED (83/83 battery, dashboard
renders end-to-end)**. Full audit of what was fixed: `finale/IMPROVEMENTS.md`.

## Decision (locked)
- Track: 1 — Merchant Growth AI
- Niche: perishable-goods micro-merchants (vegetable vendors as hero persona)
- Product: HarvestWise — voice-first AI growth copilot (WhatsApp + Paytm merchant world)
- Stack: Sarvam AI (Indic voice + LLM) + n8n (agent orchestration) + Cognee (merchant memory)
- Demo language: **Tamil primary**, English fallback (crew-fluent)

## Secrets policy
All keys live in `.env` files only — never in docs, never in chat logs, never in code.
- Sarvam / Cognee / Twilio / n8n values → `finale/.env` (template: `finale/.env.example`)
- **Keys pasted into this file during build are burned — rotate before the finale:** see `SECURITY.md`.

## Folder map
- `STATUS.md` — living mission log (phase, blockers+owners, locked decisions, eval log). Read first.
- `proof.md` — Round 1 submission evidence pack (historical record of the submitted deck).
- `knowledge/` — brief, track decision, Paytm facts, partner-stack playbook, pitch strategy, collision
  analysis, finale doctrine, verified-facts ledger (**09 = single source of truth**), prompt-engineering
  pack (10), mentor deep playbook (11).
- `deck/deck.html` + `deck/*.pdf` — the Round 1 deck and the uploaded artifact.
- `finale/` — the finale build (see `finale/README.md` for structure, endpoints and demo-safety
  switches). Start with `python finale/qa_battery.py` once the API is up.
- `.opencode/agent/hackathon-mentor.md` — Mentor agent (mode: all; also `/mentor <question>`).

## Run the finale build
```
cd finale
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env                 # add SARVAM_API_KEY
python data/seed_gen.py && python cognee/seed_memory.py
python -m uvicorn api.main:app --port 8000
start ui/index.html                  # dashboard
python qa_battery.py                 # expect 83 passed, 0 failed
```
Use **http://127.0.0.1:8000**, not `http://localhost:8000` — measured, `localhost` costs ~2 s per
request in this environment (IPv6 fallback) versus 3–35 ms for the IPv4 literal.

## Regenerate the deck PDF after editing deck.html
Open `deck/deck.html` in Edge, Ctrl+P → Save as PDF (paper size 1280x720, margins none), or use the
Edge headless command noted at the bottom of `knowledge/01`.

